{"causes": ["The expansionist policies of Napoleonic France and the subsequent humiliation of Prussia in 1806 necessitated a complete reorganization and revitalization of the Prussian military.", "His noble birth into the ancient Junker family von Kleist provided him with an inherent path into military service and instilled a strong tradition of martial duty.", "The strategic imperative for a united European front against Napoleon created opportunities for distinguished military leadership within the Sixth Coalition.", "The French Revolutionary Wars provided early combat experience that shaped his tactical understanding and leadership capabilities."], "effects": ["His decisive victory at the Battle of Kulm in 1813 significantly contributed to the unraveling of Napoleon's campaign in Central Europe.", "He was awarded the hereditary title Graf Kleist von Nollendorf, establishing a lasting legacy for his family name tied to his military achievements.", "His leadership enhanced the professional reputation of the Prussian army, contributing to a sense of national pride and military competence in the post-Napoleonic era."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "napoleonic-wars", "sourceName": "Napoleonic Wars", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "friedrich-graf-kleist-von-nollendorf", "targetName": "Friedrich Graf Kleist von Nollendorf", "context": "The widespread conflicts of the Napoleonic Wars provided the primary context and proving ground for Friedrich Graf Kleist von Nollendorf's military career from 1806 to 1814."}, {"sourceSlug": "friedrich-graf-kleist-von-nollendorf", "sourceName": "Friedrich Graf Kleist von Nollendorf", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "battle-of-kulm", "targetName": "Battle of Kulm", "context": "Friedrich Graf Kleist von Nollendorf commanded the Prussian forces that executed a crucial flanking maneuver at the Battle of Kulm on August 29-30, 1813, leading to a decisive Allied victory."}, {"sourceSlug": "friedrich-graf-kleist-von-nollendorf", "sourceName": "Friedrich Graf Kleist von Nollendorf", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "gebhard-leberecht-von-blucher", "targetName": "Gebhard Leberecht von Blücher", "context": "Kleist served under Field Marshal Blücher during the Sixth Coalition, notably in the campaign in France in 1814, contributing to the Allied advance on Paris."}, {"sourceSlug": "friedrich-graf-kleist-von-nollendorf", "sourceName": "Friedrich Graf Kleist von Nollendorf", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "prussia", "targetName": "Prussia", "context": "Friedrich Graf Kleist von Nollendorf dedicated his entire military career to the service of the Kingdom of Prussia, rising to the rank of field marshal."}, {"sourceSlug": "friedrich-graf-kleist-von-nollendorf", "sourceName": "Friedrich Graf Kleist von Nollendorf", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "prussian-military-tradition", "targetName": "Prussian Military Tradition", "context": "Kleist's exemplary service and decisive actions during the Napoleonic Wars helped cement the values of discipline, courage, and strategic initiative within the Prussian military tradition."}], "places": [{"name": "Nollendorf, Bohemia", "role": "Origin of title, Battle site"}, {"name": "Berlin, Prussia", "role": "Capital, Military career base"}, {"name": "Dresden, Saxony", "role": "Nearby major campaign city"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Friedrich Graf Kleist von Nollendorf", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "friedrich-graf-kleist-von-nollendorf"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q213784", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friedrich_Graf_Kleist_von_Nollendorf"], "tags": ["Military Leaders & Commanders", "conflict-and-resolution", "geopolitical-linkage", "empire-and-colonialism"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Friedrich Graf Kleist von Nollendorf's crucial role at the Battle of Kulm in 1813 prevented the encirclement of Allied forces and contributed significantly to the eventual defeat of Napoleon in the Sixth Coalition. He solidified the professional reputation of the Prussian military during a critical period of national reassertion.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-09-04T03:20:02Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#33832694349", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Friedrich Emil Ferdinand Heinrich von Kleist, granted the title Graf Kleist von Nollendorf from 1814 onwards, was a Prussian field marshal and a member of the old junker family von Kleist. He was a prominent figure in Prussian military during the Napoleonic Wars.", "newValue": "Friedrich Emil Ferdinand Heinrich von Kleist, later Graf Kleist von Nollendorf, emerged as a pivotal Prussian field marshal during the tumultuous Napoleonic Wars, particularly distinguished by his command at the Battle of Kulm in August 1813. A scion of the ancient Junker family von Kleist, his military career spanned the critical period of Prussian resurgence following the defeats of Jena-Auerstedt, contributing significantly to the Sixth Coalition's ultimate victory over Napoleon. His strategic acumen and steadfastness in the face of superior French forces solidified his reputation as a formidable commander and a symbol of Prussian military resilience.

Kleist's career began in the Prussian army in 1778, and he steadily rose through the ranks, participating in the Rhine Campaigns of 1793-1794. However, it was during the Wars of Liberation that he achieved his greatest renown. At the Battle of Kulm, he executed a crucial flanking maneuver, arriving from the rear to cut off and decisively defeat the French corps under General Vandamme, preventing the encirclement of a large Allied force and capturing over 10,000 prisoners. This victory, coupled with his participation in the Battle of Leipzig (1813) and the campaign in France (1814), earned him the title Graf Kleist von Nollendorf from King Frederick William III in 1814, commemorating his signal achievement.

His leadership at Kulm not only secured a vital victory but also bolstered the morale of the Allied forces and underscored the effectiveness of combined operations against the French Empire. Kleist's actions contributed to the narrative of Prussian military revival and national pride, which would later become a foundational element of German unification in the latter half of the 19th century. His legacy is enshrined in the annals of Prussian military history as a commander who, through decisive action, helped turn the tide against Napoleonic dominance in Central Europe."}, {"timestamp": "2026-09-04T03:20:02Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#33832694349", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Early Modern era: age of exploration, printing revolution, and religious reformation", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1762-04-09, Berlin"}, {"title": "Military conflicts and strategic necessities", "type": "Idea", "year": "1762-04-09, Berlin"}], "newValue": ["The expansionist policies of Napoleonic France and the subsequent humiliation of Prussia in 1806 necessitated a complete reorganization and revitalization of the Prussian military.", "His noble birth into the ancient Junker family von Kleist provided him with an inherent path into military service and instilled a strong tradition of martial duty.", "The strategic imperative for a united European front against Napoleon created opportunities for distinguished military leadership within the Sixth Coalition.", "The French Revolutionary Wars provided early combat experience that shaped his tactical understanding and leadership capabilities."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-09-04T03:20:02Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#33832694349", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Determined military outcomes shaping geopolitical boundaries", "type": "Idea", "year": "1823-02-17"}, {"title": "Contributed to global exchange networks, modern state formation, and scientific revolution", "type": "Mov